From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 08:37:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panthor: don't poll the SCMI core clock for devfreq
 status

With SCMI perf-domain DVFS (Sky1), the core clock is an SCMI clock
without a rate cache, so clk_get_rate() in panthor_devfreq_get_dev_status()
is a mailbox round trip on every devfreq poll (50 ms), on the channel the
rate-limited perf requests share. Report ptdev->current_frequency, which
the SCMI path keeps up to date; other platforms still read the clock.

Tested on a Minisforum MS-R1: no SCMI CLOCK_RATE_GET requests at idle
(with the matching amvx change; ~34/s before).

Signed-off-by: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
index 0e7bba30b..cf0278fce 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_devfreq.c
@@ -239,7 +239,13 @@ static int panthor_devfreq_get_dev_status(struct device *dev,
 	struct panthor_devfreq *pdevfreq = ptdev->devfreq;
 	unsigned long irqflags;
 
-	status->current_frequency = clk_get_rate(ptdev->clks.core);
+	/*
+	 * With SCMI DVFS the core clock is an SCMI clock without a rate cache:
+	 * clk_get_rate() is a mailbox round trip on every devfreq poll, on the
+	 * channel the perf requests share. Report the frequency we set.
+	 */
+	status->current_frequency = pdevfreq->opp_dev ? ptdev->current_frequency :
+				    clk_get_rate(ptdev->clks.core);
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&pdevfreq->lock, irqflags);
 
